    "summaryAr": "About Omni Omni is the AI analytics platform that turns company data into a trusted source of truth for AI. Built on a semantic model, Omni gives teams a governed context graph, so everyone gets the same trusted answer. Ask in plain English, refine in workbooks, or bring your data into tools like Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, and Slack. Our team has spent decades building data platforms, and we started Omni to fix problem",
    "descriptionAr": "About Omni Omni is the AI analytics platform that turns company data into a trusted source of truth for AI. Built on a semantic model, Omni gives teams a governed context graph, so everyone gets the same trusted answer. Ask in plain English, refine in workbooks, or bring your data into tools like Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, and Slack. Our team has spent decades building data platforms, and we started Omni to fix problems we saw firsthand. Today, we help customers like Condé Nast, BambooHR, and Synthesia get better answers from their data. We're headquartered in San Francisco and have raised $217M from top investors including ICONIQ, Theory Ventures, and Redpoint Ventures. Our latest $120M Series C valued us at $1.5B. If you like helping people get more from their data, come build with us. We’d love to hear from you. About the Role We are looking for an AI Engineer who will be focused on building and optimizing our agentic AI analyst, giving you the chance to tune agent behavior, measure agent performance, and add capabilities. You'll be working on a team with deep experience in the field, and you'll have the autonomy to prioritize and solve problems by yourself or in collaboration with other members of the team. All software engineers at Omni operate across our technology stack to solve customer problems, and our engineering culture is focused on shipping quickly and iteratively while maintaining high bars for performance and quality. We develop with AI and coding agents, but we expect our engineers to know when to trust their agent, when not to, and when to not even bother asking. About You Strong technical and communication skills 3-10+ years of experience building production software, proficiency in TypeScript or JavaScript Strategic thinking and the ability to balance business and product goals with velocity and engineering excellence Hands-on experience shipping LLM systems in production, working on some or all of these topics: agent harnesses, context management, retrieval, eval, or post-training. Experience doing data analysis Nice to Haves Experience building data products and AI-ready interfaces Familiarity with data warehouses like Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift Our Stack TypeScript React with Remix Kotlin / Java AWS Why Join Us Passionate, supportive team with extensive experience in the space (including founders from Looker and Stitch Data) all working together to win as a team Fully paid medical insurance for employees, plus vision and dental coverage 401(k) Plan Flexible PTO Omni is an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity and encourage you to apply even if you don’t check every single box. Please, let us know if you need any reasonable accommodations during the interview process.",
